#!/usr/bin/perl

use strict;
use Pod::Usage;
pod2usage(-exitstatus => 0, -verbose => 2);

__END__

=head1 NAME

checkEst - check and classify electronic structure theory (EST) program
output file(s) (SP, MIN, Saddle, IRC).

=head1 SYNOPSIS

I<checkEst> -e I<program> [ options ] I<infile>

=head2 Infile:

Three modes are provided:

=over 5

=item 1. I<$infile> = B<filename>; check a single output file

=item 2. I<$infile> = 'B<all>'; check all output files in the current folder

=item 3. I<$infile> = 'B<sweep>'; check + aggregate every C<sweep_*/> node
directory created by C<qesub -w> in the current folder, one row per node.

=back

=head2 Options:

=over 8

=item -h, --help    show this help message and exit

=back

=head3 B<EST related:>

=over 8

=item -e [B<g16|qchem|orca>]  assign EST program (default: B<orca>).

=item -r B<refDir>  diff extracted energy/ZPE/imaginary-frequencies and
pass/fail status against same-named reference output files in B<refDir>
(e.g. Gaussian's own shipped C<tests/amd64> reference logs). Read-only:
never writes into B<refDir>.

=item -tol B<tolerance>  absolute tolerance for the B<-r> energy/ZPE
comparison, in the units printed for that quantity (default: B<1e-6>).

=back

=head1 EXAMPLES

 Check all ORCA jobs in the current directory (default program):
 ]$ checkEst all

 Check a single Gaussian16 job:
 ]$ checkEst -e g16 molecule.log

 Check all Q-Chem jobs in the current directory:
 ]$ checkEst -e qchem all

 Check a single Gaussian16 job against a reference output:
 ]$ checkEst -e g16 -r $g16root/g16/tests/amd64 test0233.log

 Aggregate + diff every node swept by 'qesub -e g16 -w all all' against
 Gaussian's own shipped reference logs for this architecture:
 ]$ checkEst -e g16 -r $g16root/g16/tests/amd64 sweep

